WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.576
Picture a triangular playing field. You know two sides and the angle between them. How long is the third side? Pythagoras needs a right angle, so we use the cosine rule.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:29.567
The cosine rule says: a squared equals b squared plus c squared minus two b c cosine A. Side a is opposite angle A, the side the angle faces. The angle sits between b and c.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:40.993
Cosine of sixty degrees is one half. Cosine of one hundred and twenty degrees is minus one half. A negative cosine means an obtuse angle, over ninety degrees.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:54.501
Often the sides use x. Then the rule gives a quadratic, an equation with x squared in it. It can have two answers, but a length is never negative, so we may reject one.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.140
So you are asked to use the cosine rule, often to build and solve a quadratic.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:12.539
Step one: mark the known angle and the side opposite it. That side goes on the left. Step two: write the rule, with each value in brackets.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:23.547
Step three: expand every bracket and collect to zero. Step four: solve, and reject any value that makes a side negative.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:30.453
The trap is multiplying the whole bracket by cosine. The cosine belongs only to the two b c term.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:51.553
June twenty nineteen. In triangle A B C, A B is five x, B C is three x minus one, and A C is two x plus five, all in centimetres. Angle A B C is sixty degrees. Find x, to three significant figures. Five marks.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:59.632
Angle B is between A B and B C. So the side opposite is A C. It goes on the left of the rule.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:07.445
Step two: write the rule. Cosine of sixty degrees is a half, so the two and the half cancel.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:19.649
Step three: expand every bracket. The left is four x squared plus twenty x plus twenty five. The right collects to nineteen x squared minus x plus one.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:28.502
Collect to one side, then divide by three. This gives five x squared minus seven x minus eight, equals zero.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:43.739
Use the formula: seven plus or minus root two hundred and nine, over ten. So x is two point one four five seven, or minus nought point seven four five seven. A negative x makes B C negative, so reject it.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:52.658
A tempting route multiplies the whole bracket by a half. That gives only negative answers, so it cannot be right.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:03:01.128
So x is two point one five, to three significant figures. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:16.738
A common mistake is squaring each term of a bracket. Three x minus one, all squared, is nine x squared minus six x plus one. Missing the middle term makes the quadratic wrong.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:29.421
Now you try, from January twenty twenty three. Find x in the form p plus q root three. Write your answer, then choose Continue to Answer.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:43.101
The opposite side is Y Z. Write the rule. Expanding gives four x squared minus four x plus one, equals three x squared plus twelve x plus twelve.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:57.655
Solve: sixteen plus or minus root three hundred, over two. Root three hundred is ten root three. So x is eight plus or minus five root three. Eight minus five root three is negative, so reject it.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:05.279
A common wrong answer keeps both roots. A length cannot be negative, and the answer must be in the form asked.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.065
Remember: opposite side, rule, expand, solve, reject.
